We have applied Ensemble Kalman Inversion (EKI) combined with level-set parameterizations to infer subsurface electrical properties from Electrical Resistivity Tomography (ERT) data [@Tso1], and subsequently extended this framework to Induced Polarization measurements [@Tso2]. Our numerical experiments demonstrate that, in contrast to standard smoothness-constrained optimization approaches, the level-set formulation enables more accurate identification of interfaces between different lithofacies.

